Run these in both SIT and UAT. They are read-only and demonstrate the pipeline clearly.

## 1. Show table coverage and freshness

```sql
SELECT
    'ORIGINAL CTR' AS table_name,
    COUNT(*) AS total_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT contact_id) AS distinct_contacts,
    MIN(last_update_timestamp) AS earliest_timestamp,
    MAX(last_update_timestamp) AS latest_timestamp
FROM public.ctr

UNION ALL

SELECT
    'CTR FLATTENED' AS table_name,
    COUNT(*) AS total_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT contact_id) AS distinct_contacts,
    MIN(last_update_timestamp) AS earliest_timestamp,
    MAX(last_update_timestamp) AS latest_timestamp
FROM public.ctr_flattened;
```

Explain:

> “The original CTR table can contain multiple versions of a Contact ID, while the flattened table is intended to retain one latest version per Contact ID.”

