## 6. Demonstrate latest-version selection

This finds Contact IDs that have multiple original versions and compares them with the single flattened version:

```sql
WITH multi_version_contacts AS (
    SELECT
        contact_id,
        COUNT(*) AS original_version_count,
        MAX(last_update_timestamp) AS expected_latest_timestamp
    FROM public.ctr
    WHERE contact_id IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY contact_id
    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
)
SELECT
    m.contact_id,
    m.original_version_count,
    m.expected_latest_timestamp,
    f.last_update_timestamp AS flattened_timestamp,
    CASE
        WHEN f.last_update_timestamp = m.expected_latest_timestamp
            THEN 'LATEST VERSION RETAINED'
        ELSE 'CHECK REQUIRED'
    END AS result
FROM multi_version_contacts m
JOIN public.ctr_flattened f
    ON m.contact_id = f.contact_id
ORDER BY m.original_version_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

This is a good demo query because it visibly proves the purpose of the pipeline.

